2
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:42,000
The Incredible Hulk is a science fiction, action,
adventure film directed by Louis Leterrier.

3
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Scientist Bruce Banner scours the planet for an antidote to the
unbridled force of rage within him: the Hulk.

4
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:18,000
But when the military masterminds who dream of exploiting his powers force him back to
civilization, he finds himself coming face to face with a new, deadly foe.

5
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Bruce Banner, played by Edward Norton.

6
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Betty Ross, played by Liv Tyler.

7
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:42,000
Emil Blonsky, played by Tim Roth.

8
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:30,000
General 'Thunderbolt' Ross, played by William Hurt.

9
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Samuel Sterns, played by Tim Blake Nelson.

10
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Leonard, played by Ty Burrell.

11
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:54,000
The Incredible Hulk is a 2008 American superhero film based
on the Marvel Comics character the Hulk.

12
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:42,000
Produced by Marvel Studios and Valhalla Motion Pictures, and distributed by Universal
Pictures, it is the second film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

13
00:49:24,000 --> 00:49:30,000
It was directed by Louis Leterrier from a screenplay by Zak Penn, and stars Edward Norton as Bruce Banner
alongside Liv Tyler, Tim Roth, William Hurt, Tim Blake Nelson, Ty Burrell, and Christina Cabot.

14
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:18,000
In the film, Banner becomes the monstrous Hulk as an unwitting pawn in a military
scheme to reinvigorate the "super soldier" program through gamma radiation.

15
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
He goes on the run from the military while
attempting to cure himself of the Hulk.

16
01:00:48,000 --> 01:00:54,000
After the mixed reception to Universal's 2003 film Hulk, Marvel Studios reacquired the
rights to the character, though Universal retained distribution rights.

17
01:04:36,000 --> 01:04:42,000
Leterrier, who expressed interest in directing Iron Man (2008) for Marvel, was brought onboard and
Penn wrote a script that was closer to the comics and the 1978–1982 television series.

18
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:30,000
In April 2007, Norton was hired to portray Banner
and to rewrite Penn's screenplay.

19
01:12:12,000 --> 01:12:18,000
His script positioned the film as a reboot of the series, distancing it
from the 2003 film to give the new version its own identity.

20
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Norton was ultimately not credited for his writing.

21
01:19:48,000 --> 01:19:54,000
Filming took place from July to November 2007, primarily in Toronto, with
additional filming in New York City and Rio de Janeiro.

22
01:23:36,000 --> 01:23:42,000
Over 700 visual effects shots were created in post-production using a
combination of motion capture and computer-generated imagery.

23
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
The Incredible Hulk premiered at the Gibson Amphitheatre in Universal City, California, on June 8,
2008, and was released in the United States on June 13, as part of Phase One of the MCU.

24
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
It received praise for its action sequences and was considered an improvement
over the 2003 film, but it was criticized as lacking in depth.

25
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
The film grossed $265.6 million worldwide.

26
01:38:48,000 --> 01:38:54,000
Norton and Marvel Studios had various production disagreements while working on the film,
including over the final edit, which Marvel Studios deemed uncollaborative.

27
01:42:36,000 --> 01:42:42,000
Norton was replaced in the role of Banner by Mark Ruffalo for
subsequent MCU appearances starting with The Avengers in 2012.

28
